{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact clean head 95374ec2b44779fc712de97c0bec4270c94b9fcb.\n\nARCHITECTURE. The change affects layer 7 composition/transport and UI, with ordinary local Git configuration as input. Kernel, host binding, the Workroom interpreter, and the durable projection are unchanged, and the code preserves dependency direction. But the surface/UI contract changes: /v0/worktrees gains an optional remote and the browser gains navigation from local Git configuration. This exact head does not update docs/reference/architecture.md or publish its candidate artifact, as the review rule requires. It also leaves explicit exhaustive claims false in docs/reference/gs/serve.md under Local worktrees and docs/concepts/components.md under the resident worktree description. Update and re-anchor those pages in the repaired head.\n\nSECURITY. The dual http/https allowlists, required host, userinfo refusal, parser serialization, React escaping, rel=noopener noreferrer, and name-before-filter selection are sound. One trust-boundary defect blocks approval: gitRemotes invokes git config without --local, so command/global config contributes remote.origin.url. I reproduced this with GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: the legitimate local origin is emitted first, an injected https origin second, and the last-write-wins map exposes the injected URL; adding --local returns only the repository origin. Read repository-local configuration and add a regression that injects an outer-scope origin and proves it cannot reach LocalRepo, /v0/worktrees, or an href. Bound remote enumeration and URL/config output so valid oversized configuration fails closed. Also either reject query and fragment at both layers or state and test the narrower credential policy: today access_token query/fragment material reaches the API, DOM, and href despite the secret-exclusion rationale. Add a genuinely unknown authority-bearing scheme such as future+git://host/repo so replacing the allowlist with an enumerated denylist fails.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. Keep the browser-side check: it is a small, justified second decision at the href boundary and protects against older residents and future callers. repolink.ts is already the smallest clear form, and the app/service/render tests cover distinct seams; I found no simplification change beyond the requested fixes.\n\nINDEPENDENT GATES. HEAD and origin/request/repo-remote-link both equal 95374ec2 and the worktree is clean. go test ./... -count=1 passed, npm test --prefix ui passed 95/95, go build ./... and go vet ./... passed, make ui-check reproduced the committed embed, and git diff --check passed. Do not merge this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d8c2e96d67308017207d1a9a5806a46d12c698ab","dead_basis_override":"true","head":"95374ec2b44779fc712de97c0bec4270c94b9fcb","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2a6548c5c32e3437e643ebb96748ef6d81850ecc\",\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3ba67ffaaa581d6faf814e5345932fdf68ed979e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6160928d8865ffda044f7f25e471d7ab6d375f7e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}